title: karr delete without --yes prints Perl warnings when stdin is not a TTY
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

Exactly the class of bug ticket #33 was:

    karr delete 2 < /dev/null
    Use of uninitialized value $answer in scalar chomp at Cmd/Delete.pm line 70.
    Use of uninitialized value $answer in pattern match (m//) at Cmd/Delete.pm line 71.
    Delete task 2: d? [y/N] Skipped task 2: d
    rc=0

`my $answer = <STDIN>` (`Cmd/Delete.pm:69-71`) returns undef at EOF. Any agent or
CI run that forgets `--yes` gets raw Perl diagnostics on stderr.

Fix: treat EOF as "no" without warning — and consider refusing outright with a
clear "not a terminal, use --yes" message, which is friendlier to the unattended
agents karr is built for. Check the other interactive prompts for the same
pattern (`restore`, `destroy`).
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
